    "title": "The Leadership Operating System",
    "paragraphs": [
      "The elevator is most useful when it becomes a recurring management rhythm rather than a one-time lesson.\n35. A Weekly Leadership Review\nUse a weekly review to inspect the quality of leadership and the health of the operating system.\nDirection\n- Are the current priorities clear?\n- Has anything changed that requires a decision?\n- Are teams spending time on the most important work?\nDelegation\n- Are assignments SMART?\n- Do owners have the authority and resources they need?\n- Which tasks are bouncing back to the leader?\n- Is the leader taking work back unnecessarily?\nCommunication\n- Are meetings ending with decisions, owners, and dates?\n- Are problems being framed accurately?\n- Are updates concise and clear?\n- Are unresolved risks visible?\nPeople\n- Are critical roles filled by people with the required evidence?\n- Are strong performers being supported?\n- Are performance problems being addressed promptly?\n- Is the team carrying avoidable underperformance?\nIncentives and culture\n- Are rewards aligned with outcomes?\n- Are meetings consuming too much time?\n- Is good work being recognised?\n- Are capable people receiving meaningful responsibility and access?\n- Are standards applied consistently?\nSystems\n- Which important processes still depend on one person?\n- What needs to be documented or automated?\n- Where is a backup owner needed?\n- What would fail if a key person were unavailable?\n36. A Monthly People and Performance Review\nFor each team or function, review:\n1. The outcomes the team is responsible for.\n2. The people who are consistently producing those outcomes.\n3. The capability gaps affecting performance.\n4. The roles that need clearer ownership.\n5. The work that should stop or be simplified.\n6. The employees ready for greater responsibility.\n7. The standards or behaviours that need attention.\n8. The systems that are creating recurring problems.\nAvoid turning this into a ranking exercise detached from context. Use evidence, understand constraints, and consider the quality of the work as well as the numbers.\n37. A Quarterly Owner Review\nAt the owner level, review:\n- Whether the business is moving toward its stated vision.\n- Whether the most important strategic decisions were made well.\n- Whether resources are allocated to the right priorities.\n- Whether the leadership team can operate independently.\n- Whether key-person dependencies have decreased.\n- Whether the organisation is rewarding the behaviours it wants.\n- Whether the founder or CEO is still the bottleneck.\n- Which systems must be strengthened before the next stage of growth."
    ]
